1. Convert a list to an array
using toArray() method
List<Integer> numbers=List.of(1,2,3,4,5);
a) Object [] objArr=numbers.toArray();//no parameter specified then object array
b) Integer[] numbersArray=numbers.toArray(new Integer[0]);//parameter specified for particular type
c) Integer [] numbersArray=numbers.stream().toArray(Integer[]::new); //using stream api

All these 3 ways will create only wrapper objects not primitive
a) If we need primitive either we convert the wrapper objects to primitive using for loop
int[] primitiveArray = new int[numbersArray.length];
for (int i = 0; i < numbersArray.length; i++) {
    primitiveArray[i] = numbersArray[i];  // Unboxing the Integer to int
}

b) Using stream to convert primitive
int[] primitiveArray = numbers.stream().mapToInt(Integer::intValue).toArray();
long[] longArray = numbers.stream().mapToLong(Integer::longValue).toArray();
double[] doubleArray = numbers.stream().mapToDouble(Integer::doubleValue).toArray();

